            "finalAnswer": "$0.75$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "A negative angle can still give a positive tan; locate the quadrant first."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ch14_ex3_q2g",
          "number": "2(g)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "Use a calculator to find, correct to two decimal places: $\\tan 239^\\circ$",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "$\\tan(180^\\circ + \\theta) = \\tan\\theta$",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $239^\\circ$. Goal: $\\tan 239^\\circ$ to 2 d.p.",
              "Degree mode: $\\tan 239^\\circ = 1.6642\\ldots$",
              "Check: $239^\\circ = 180^\\circ + 59^\\circ$, so $\\tan 239^\\circ = \\tan 59^\\circ \\approx 1.66$ (as in Example 7). ✓",
              "So $\\tan 239^\\circ \\approx 1.66$."
